//! A `sameTerm` between two columns is enforced where the two columns first meet (0.6.2): within
//! one scan as a term-id compare, across a join as a join key, and nowhere else is the filter
//! moved. The same scan constraint enforces a
//! variable repeated within one triple pattern (`?x :r ?x`, `?x ?p ?x`, `GRAPH ?g { ?g ?p ?g }`),
//! which 0.6.1 never checked: it returned every triple of the predicate.
//!
//! Every case's rows are rdflib's, the SPARQL text's answer (generated by `gen.py` from one
//! dataset); each case also states what its plan must show, by the rule above.
//!
//! ```bash
//! cargo test -p grafeo-engine --all-features --test main sparql_equality_pushdown::
//! ```

#![cfg(feature = "sparql")]

